WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.750
E-cigarettes and heated tobacco sound modern, clean and less harmful than cigarettes.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.750
In reality, they are a new danger, especially for young people.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.250
Many users don't know that besides nicotine, e-liquids can also contain synthetic drugs,

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:22.550
causing psychotic episodes, loss of control, even hospitalization.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.550
Sadly, most of these cases are school and university students.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:33.050
Although they are completely banned, many young people still find ways to use them.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.750
The danger is not only addiction, but harmful substances hidden behind fragrant smoke.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:44.250
Here is what was recorded at Bach Mai Hospital.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.450
Doctors at the Poison Control Center filmed these images during emergency care.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.150
This 27-year-old patient had used e-cigarettes for more than two years.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:59.650
He arrived extremely agitated; repeated sedatives and antipsychotics could not control him.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:12.750
Doctors had to anesthetize him and put him on a ventilator for several days.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.350
Tests of the patients' e-liquids found at least three synthetic drugs,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:23.350
some so new they had never been recorded in Vietnam before.
